{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>Then they shall accept their iniquity.</b> From here the Rabbis, blessed be their memory, derived that suffering atones just as sacrifices atone: it is written here ״ואז ירצו את עונם״, and it is written of sacrifices (Leviticus 1:4) ״ונרצה לו לכפר עליו״ — and not only that, but sacrifices involve money while suffering involves the body."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:51.646391367Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}